  "decision_summary": "Strengthen high: L6 hepatic-clearance/metabolic-stability records do not provide affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F<20%. Measurable hepatic metabolism/clearance in high-F precedents (erythromycin 25-36.5%, idarubicin ~30%, hydrocortisone ~96%) shows that first-pass liability is compatible with F>=20. Simvastatin/triptolide metabolism records are poorly transferable to the tert-butyl trilactone query. Direct absolute-F precedents from neutral/polar rigid polycyclic compounds remain predominantly >=20%, and bilobalide Caco-2 permeability is moderate. Confidence remains moderate due to lack of query-specific data and the query's very low logD/high TPSA."
}

